{
	"_comment": "Cross-language conformance table for the move-grading rule in shared/classification.json. Run through BOTH implementations — server/app/analysis.py::classify_move (server/tests/test_classification.py) and client/src/lib/classification.ts::classifyMove (client/src/lib/classification.test.ts) — so a threshold change or an off-by-one in either one fails immediately. Evals are white's point of view: cp clamped, mate signed for White (0 = mate on the board, cp says who gave it). `clampCases` and `winPercentCases` do the same for the clamp and the winning-chances curve.",
	"cases": [
		{
			"before": {
				"cp": 0
			},
			"after": {
				"cp": 0
			},
			"moverIsWhite": true,
